<h2 id=3D"optimization---bottom-up">Optimization - Bottom Up</h2>
<p>An important thing to notice is that in the DP solution, we only ever ne=
ed to access the previous two values of the DP array (at <code>i - 1</code>=
 and <code>i - 2</code>) to calculate the current value (at <code>i</code>)=
. This means we don=E2=80=99t need to store the entire DP array.</p>
<p>Instead, we can use two variables to keep track of the previous two valu=
es:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>one_step_before</code>: to store the value of <code>dp[i - 1]</co=
de>.</li>
<li><code>two_steps_before</code>: to store the value of <code>dp[i - 2]</c=
ode>.</li>
</ul>
<p>As we iterate through the steps, we update these two variables to always=
 hold the values for the previous two steps. This approach retains the time=
 complexity of <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math xml=
ns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo st=
retchy=3D"false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo></mrow><annot=
ation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math></=
span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"><=
span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span=
><span class=3D"mord mathnormal" style=3D"margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span=
><span class=3D"mopen">(</span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span><spa=
n class=3D"mclose">)</span></span></span></span>, while reducing space comp=
lexity to <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D=
"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretch=
y=3D"false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo></mrow><annotation=
